				"A 6‑second portrait‑mode short video in a real mobile‑phone filming style. The main subject is a young woman performing gentle, natural dance movements in an indoor room.\n\nCharacter Appearance:\nYoung woman with long black hair naturally falling over her shoulders, light and natural makeup, fresh and pure气质. She wears a loose white long‑sleeved top and light gray denim shorts, presenting a casual, youthful, energetic short‑video outfit style suitable for everyday life.\n\nScene Environment:\nIndoor bedroom or apartment space, with warm‑colored walls, a glass sliding door, and simple furniture. Warm yellow overhead lighting keeps the space clean and tidy. The setting remains a real residential environment—no studio feel.\n\nMovement Design:\nThe person stands facing the camera, with a naturally relaxed posture.\n\nStart:\nThe woman gently sways her body, hands naturally placed in front, wrists making subtle dance movements, while wearing a natural smile and looking at the camera.\n\nMiddle:\nShe slowly turns her body sideways, creating slight undulations in her shoulders and waist, with her hips naturally swaying to the rhythm. Her right hand lightly lifts to adjust her hair or make a simple gesture, and her long hair flows naturally with the body’s turn.\n\nEnd:\nShe returns to facing the camera, continuing to sway gently left and right, with hands crossed or close to the front of her body, maintaining a sweet and natural expression.\n\nCamera Language:\nPortrait‑mode phone filming, fixed camera position, medium‑to‑full‑body framing with the camera at about waist height, keeping the full figure in view. No significant zooms, pans, or cuts.\n\nPhotographic Effect:\nRealistic phone‑camera texture, slight wide‑angle perspective, indoor warm lighting, natural skin tone, authentic hair and fabric texture, subtle motion blur, and a casual short‑video feel.\n\nOverall Style:\nA realistic self‑shot dance video, capturing a young woman’s daily life, fresh and natural—not a commercial studio production, not animated, not CG."
